  "text": "[patient] Hello doctor, I have small red bumps on the penile head since a week. They occurred possibly after I took antibiotics for tonsil infection. It caused acidity. It started with mild itching on penile head. The itching subsided after a couple of days, but the small red bumps are still present. They are accompanied by a mildly bad odor and sometimes thick white scattered dry discharge. Retracting the foreskin is not painful and there is no burning sensation. I had unprotected intercourse with my long time partner after a substantial gap. The itching started before 15 to 20 days without any discharge. Every day, I clean the genitals with normal soap from outside and even after urinating I clean it from tap water. Kindly advise on the course to be followed. Thank you.\n[doctor] Hi. Revert back with the photos to a urologist online -->https://www.icliniq.com/ask-a-doctor-online/urologist",
